{
  "id": "jarvis-visible-agent-orchestrator",
  "name": "Jarvis - Visible Agent Orchestrator",
  "active": true,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Jarvis Native Agent runtime\n\nJarvis Chat, Telegram, or Open WebUI posts to this workflow. The request now goes directly into the n8n AI Agent. The agent uses local Ollama as the default/fallback model and specialist agent tools for capabilities.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "note-overview",
      "name": "Jarvis Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1120,
        -540
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Workflow levels\n\nL0 answer_only: chat answer\nL1 draft_or_plan: drafts, plans, summaries\nL2 state/private data: tasks, calendar, contacts, homelab\nL3 external/spend: sending, publishing, expenses\nL4 danger_zone: destructive/public/payment/delete",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 360
      },
      "id": "note-levels",
      "name": "Workflow Level Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -240,
        -540
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "Free/open-source worker targets\n\nTasks: Vikunja, CalDAV VTODO, or local SQLite\nCalendar: Radicale/CalDAV or Google Calendar\nEmail: IMAP/SMTP, Mailrise, or Gmail\nContacts: Radicale/CardDAV\nExpenses: Actual Budget or local sheet\nVoice: local Whisper Worker\nHomelab: Home Assistant + internal APIs",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "note-tools",
      "name": "Worker Tool Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        620,
        -540
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "jarvis/n8n/agent",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "intake-webhook",
      "name": "Jarvis Chat / Telegram Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -1120,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "jarvis-visible-agent"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const body = $json.body || $json;\nconst request = String(body.request || body.message || body.text || body.prompt || body.goal || '').trim();\nreturn [{ json: {\n  request,\n  source: body.source || body.chat_source || 'jarvis-chat',\n  capability: body.capability || '',\n  inputs: body.inputs || {},\n  limits: body.limits || { maximum_runtime_seconds: 1800, maximum_cost_usd: 0 },\n  permissions: body.permissions || { may_execute: false, may_publish: false },\n  conversation_id: body.conversation_id || body.chat_id || 'default',\n  received_at: new Date().toISOString()\n}}];"
      },
      "id": "normalize-message",
      "name": "Normalize Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -880,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{JSON.stringify($json)}}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 202
        }
      },
      "id": "respond",
      "name": "Reply to Jarvis Chat / Telegram",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        80,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "note-native-agent",
      "name": "Native Agentic Layer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1120,
        -980
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Active Jarvis Agent Runtime\nWebhook -> Normalize -> Jarvis Native Agent -> Format Response -> Reply.\n\nRouting belongs to Jarvis Native Agent. Specialist capabilities are exposed as AI Agent Tools, not a Capability Switch.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 360,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-agent-tools",
      "name": "Specialist MCP Tool Ring",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -260,
        -980
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Specialist Agent Tools\nJarvis has these tools: Drafting, Tasks, Calendar, Email, Contacts, Expenses, Voice/Whisper, Homelab, Code.\n\nEach tool uses local Ollama as model fallback and can call its own MCP/tool cluster as credentials are added.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 360,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-mcp-servers",
      "name": "Worker MCP Server Zones",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        640,
        -980
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Worker MCP servers\nEach box below is where we wire real service tools. Start free/open-source: Vikunja/Radicale/CardDAV/IMAP/Actual Budget/Home Assistant/Whisper. Google/Gmail can be swapped in later.",
        "width": 860,
        "height": 360,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "native-jarvis-agent",
      "name": "Jarvis Native Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "position": [
        -520,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "={{ $json.request }}",
        "promptType": "define",
        "hasOutputParser": false,
        "needsFallback": false,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are Jarvis, Kadin's private homelab personal assistant. You are the supervisor agent and you decide which specialist tool to call. Use local Ollama by default. For email: drafting is safe and should produce a draft; sending/replying/searching email requires explicit approval and a configured email tool. For tasks/calendar/contacts/expenses/homelab/code/voice, call the specialist tool when helpful. If a specialist tool is not configured yet, still answer using your local model and clearly say what connector is needed. Keep responses concise and useful. Do not expose hidden chain-of-thought; provide a short visible plan or result when useful. Current time: {{ $now }}."
        }
      }
    },
